+# PlacementRules spec cleanup
+
+`PlacementRules.spec.luau` goes from 31 tests to 21. Every rule in the `PlacementRules.luau`
+doc comments is still covered, and the two rules that had no test now have one. The tests only
+use the public API (`snap`, `validate`, `MaxHeight`, `MaxReach`) and `BlockTypes.BlockSize`,
+so a refactor that keeps behavior the same should no longer break them. `PlacementRules.luau` is
+unchanged.
+
+## The two failing tests
+
+- **"rejects a position that isn't a Vector3"** called matchers with a colon
+  (`expect(ok):toBe(false)`). Jest Roblox matchers are dot-called, so the test errored instead
+  of asserting. Fixed and moved into the bad-position table.
+- **"doesn't mark the cell occupied"** asserted `expect(count).toBeFalsy()` with `count = 0`.
+  In Luau `0` is truthy, so this always failed. It now checks the `occupied` table directly.
+
+A third test, **"rejects placing twice in the same cell"**, only passed because the test before
+it had written into a shared file-level `occupied` table. Run alone, it failed. The shared table
+is gone and every test builds its own state.
+
+## Removed
+
+| Test | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `snap` "snaps positions to cell centers" | Computed the expected value with the same formula as the code, so it could never fail. |
+| `snap` rows `(1,1,1)` and `(2,2,2)` | Same case as the `(0,0,0)` row: a point inside the first cell. |
+| `_isFinite` x3 | Tested a private helper exposed only for the spec. NaN and infinity are now covered through `validate`, so inlining or renaming the helper no longer breaks the suite. (`PlacementRules._isFinite` is now unused, but this change leaves the module alone.) |
+| "accepts a $Name block" (5 rows, built at runtime from `BlockTypes.List`) | `validate` treats every block type the same, so one accepted name is enough. It is covered by the valid-placement test. |
+| "returns the snapped center" | Expected `PlacementRules.snap(position)`, which is tautological. Merged into the valid-placement test, which now expects a hand-worked center. |
+| "calls snap exactly once" | Spied on an internal call count. This is the test most likely to break on a refactor that keeps behavior. |
+| "rejects placing twice in the same cell" | Duplicate of "rejects a cell that is already occupied", and it depended on test order. |
+| `BlockTypes` "has the right block types" | Restated catalog data field by field (colors, materials, transparency). No rule says those values are fixed, so any art tweak broke it. It also didn't belong in this module's spec. |
+
+## Changed
+
+- **Snap table**: 5 rows written as fractions of `BlockSize`. The rows are a cell's lower
+  corner, just below the next cell, exactly on the next cell's corner, just below zero, and one
+  row with different values per axis so each axis is checked on its own.
+- **Height table**: rows are now built from `MaxHeight`, not hard-coded 196/200. The four rows
+  sit just below the Baseplate, on the Baseplate, half a cell under `MaxHeight`, and half a cell
+  over it. The root stands at the position, so reach never affects these rows.
+- **Reach table**: rows were literals that assumed `BlockSize = 4`. They are now
+  "exactly `MaxReach`" (accepted, the documented inclusive edge) and "just past `MaxReach`"
+  (rejected). The well-inside row was dropped because it is the same case as the exact edge.
+- **Rejection reasons**: tests no longer compare the reason strings. The doc only promises
+  "a short reason for the server log", so tests check that a string comes back. Each rejection
+  test changes one input from a placement that is otherwise accepted, so the result still shows
+  which rule did the rejecting.
+- **Bad input**: `validate` writes its own guards, so there is one row per branch. Block type has
+  two rows (unknown name, not a string). Position has four rows (not a Vector3, NaN, infinity,
+  negative infinity), with each bad value on a different axis.
+- The spec now follows the project style: `--!strict`, `const`, and `@game/...` string requires.
+
+## Added (rules that had no test)
+
+- "rejects a player with no character" (`rootPosition == nil`).
+- "leaves occupied unchanged when it accepts a placement". The old test checked the empty-table
+  case with a broken assertion.
+
+## Assumptions and notes for review
+
+- Specs can't run in this environment. luau-lsp (strict), selene, and StyLua pass. The edge
+  values were worked out by hand against the current tuning (`BlockSize = 4`, `MaxHeight = 200`,
+  `MaxReach = 24`). The first CI or Studio run is the real check.
+- The doc comment says a cell must be "above the Baseplate (Y > 0)", but the code rejects
+  `center.Y < 0`. Cell centers are always odd multiples of `BlockSize / 2`, so no center can be
+  exactly 0 and the two agree in practice. For the same reason, whether `MaxHeight` itself is
+  inclusive can't be tested with the current tuning. I left both as they are, since this change
+  doesn't touch the module.
+- I would normally confirm the cut list before making it. Nobody was available, so I went ahead
+  using the rules above: one test per behavior, test at the public API, and no restating data.
+- `BlockTypes` has no spec of its own now. If its invariants matter (unique names, `ByName`
+  matching `List`), they belong in a separate `BlockTypes.spec.luau` that loops over the entries
+  and collects offenders.
